hi George Herbert Walker Bush it was the  pinnacle of his political career his  inauguration as president in 1989 I'll  help meager in graduation by his side  Barbara the love of his life  and what a life long eventful and  remarkable in so many ways born in the  optimistic America of the 20s he was  raised in a large affluent family his  father a senator passing on a tradition  of public service at 18 he was the  Navy's youngest fighter pilot in the  Second World War flying combat missions  in the South Pacific including one where  he had to be rescued by a u.s. submarine  in shark-infested waters after being hit  by Japanese anti-aircraft fire he went  into the oil business  it made him a millionaire and a  political career beckoned first standing  for Congress strengthened the United  Nations and later becoming US ambassador  to the United Nations and also director  of the CIA after two terms as vice  president to Ronald Reagan he campaigned  for the top job with a famous mantra  read my lips  his promise not to raise taxes backfired  when having won the presidency who did  just that  but his term was dominated by world  events the fall of the Berlin Wall the  collapse of the Soviet Union and most  memorably war in the Gulf as I report to  you air attacks are underway against  military targets in Iraq Operation  Desert Storm followed the invasion of  Kuwait by Iraqi forces in 1990 air  strikes and a ground attack to remove  Saddam's forces from Kuwait led to the  surrender of many Iraqi troops and a  ceasefire within weeks Bush was later  criticized for not pushing on to Baghdad  to remove Saddam from power he felt it  would cost too many lives the decision  seemed popular at the time but the  economy fell into recession and Bush  paid the price when challenged by Bill  Clinton in 1992 an independent Ross  Perot also took votes from Bush  he maintained an active life even  skydiving regularly to mark special  birthdays and he pursued his love of  sports usually with Barbara right  alongside but gradually his health  declined and he developed a form of  Parkinson's disease when Barbara died it  took quite a toll and ended the longest  marriage of any presidential couple in  US history 73 years her funeral attended  by former presidents and their wives  George HW Bush was also the longest  living president in American history it  was an extraordinary life mark Osteen  Sky News
 

